    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d229">

                <pb facs="0680" n="1310" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg1310"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1" type="from"
                            >Fish</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_RB1" type="to"
                            >Beardsley</persName></hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 28,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 55.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 76, of the 24th ultimo,
                    relative to the case of Leopold Ungar, has been received. In reply I have to
                    state that, supposing him to have been duly naturalized, it is manifest, from
                    the facts which you state, that as he has never discharged any duty of a citizen
                    of the United States, and probably lived abroad during the whole of the late
                    civil war, he has morally if not legally forfeited all claim to interference in
                    his behalf by this Government.</p>
                <p>If, however, he should be charged with an offense against Prussian law for which
                    his extradition for trial in Prussia may be granted, as our <pb facs="0681"
                        n="1311" xml:id="pg1311"/> treaty with Prussia as well as that with Great
                    Britain does not exempt us from surrendering even native citizens who, in such
                    cases, may seek refuge at home, we cannot properly object to the giving up of
                    Ungar by the government of a foreign country. Your course on the occasion is
                    approved.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_HF1">HAMILTON FISH</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
